[SECTION]
TITLE: Executive Summary

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This Software Accomplishment Summary provides evidence that the Flight Management System software has been developed in accordance with DO-178C requirements for Design Assurance Level A software. This document demonstrates compliance with the Plan for Software Aspects of Certification (PSAC) and serves as the primary compliance artifact for certification.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1. Software Identification

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
**Part Number:** FMS-SW-2024-001
**Software Version:** 2.1.0
**Configuration Index:** SCI-FMS-2.1.0
**CRC Checksum:** 0xA5F3C2D1

This software version has been verified and is ready for certification and operational use.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2. System Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Flight Management System (FMS) is an integrated avionics system providing automated flight control, navigation, and performance management for commercial aircraft. The system interfaces with GPS, IRS, air data sensors, and flight control systems to optimize flight operations.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3. Software Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The FMS software consists of navigation management, guidance control, performance calculation, database management, and display interface components. The software implements spatial and temporal partitioning to isolate Level A critical functions from lower-level components.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4. Certification Considerations

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software is certified to **Design Assurance Level A** per DO-178C.

This classification is based on the system safety assessment which determined that software failures could lead to catastrophic failure conditions affecting aircraft navigation and flight control.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 5. Software Life Cycle

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software was developed using a modified V-model lifecycle as defined in the Software Development Plan (SDP). All software lifecycle processes defined in DO-178C have been applied:

- Software Planning Process
- Software Development Process
- Software Verification Process
- Software Configuration Management Process
- Software Quality Assurance Process
<<<

[/SECTION]

